# Repositories (re)created under ~/work on every `make provision`.
# One per line:  <name> [git-url] [remote-add options]
# <name> becomes ~/work/<name>. Blank lines and # comments are ignored. Applied
# by bootstrap.sh step_remotes, which runs remote-add for each entry
# (idempotent). Policy: one Remote Control server, `work` (~/work, capacity 2,
# claude-remote.service); sessions started there are steered from the
# operator's machine, so the entries are `--clone-only`. Drop the flag on a
# line to give that project its own server (claude-remote@<name>).
workbench https://github.com/msavdert/workbench.git --clone-only
ai-hub https://github.com/msavdert/ai-hub.git --clone-only
dba-to-dbre https://github.com/msavdert/dba-to-dbre.git --clone-only
suhuf https://github.com/msavdert/suhuf.git --clone-only
# private second-brain repo: written to by hermes (00-inbox) and the nightly
# vault-compile timer; brain sessions live on the mac (vault HANDOFF D7/D9)
vault https://github.com/msavdert/vault.git --clone-only
# found running as per-project servers on 2026-09-01 (started by hand with
# remote-add, never listed here): clone-only keeps the checkouts across a
# rebuild; whether each deserves its own server is the operator's call
agentshard https://github.com/msavdert/agentshard.git --clone-only
dipladder https://github.com/msavdert/dipladder.git --clone-only
dryrun https://github.com/msavdert/dryrun.git --clone-only
quant-research https://github.com/msavdert/quant-research.git --clone-only
traderx https://github.com/msavdert/traderx.git --clone-only
